"""hawkeye-devnet: real regtest ycashd nodes + anvil with wYEC + one Hawkeye per attestor (plan H6).

The success criterion of plan §9: Hawkeye runs as a sidecar next to a real `ycashd`. This script
starts N+1 regtest nodes (node0 = the user: miner, depositor, wYEC holder; node1..N = attestors),
activates the vault upgrade (`-nuparams=6d5b7a31:<h>`), creates the attestor set with the plan §2
regtest row, enrols one member key per attestor node, deploys wYEC on anvil with those members'
Ethereum addresses as guardians (eth/script/Deploy.s.sol), writes one hawkeye.toml per attestor and
starts `hawkeye run` beside each attestor's own node. Each Hawkeye talks only to its own node.

The commands mirror bridge-sim's (ycash-dd contrib/yellowback/devnet/bridge-sim) so the two can be
compared: up | lock | burn | rogue | silence | unsilence | mine | pause | resume | status | logs |
cli | down | clean | scenario demo | roll | dormancy | takeover | double | restart | reorg.  Python 3 standard library only; Foundry (anvil, forge, cast)
on PATH.

Environment:
  YCASHD, YCASH_CLI   the node binaries, built from ycash-dd `upgrade/vault` (devnet/README.md);
                      default: `ycashd` / `ycash-cli` on PATH
  DEVNET_NODE_LINE    ycash-dd | ycash6: the node line (its start-up args, the transcript name);
                      default: read from `ycashd -version` (major version >= 6 is ycash6)
  HAWKEYE             the daemon binary (default: <repo>/target/debug/hawkeye)
  HAWKEYE_DEVNET_FALLBACK=1
                      use this script's own lock/burn/rogue/enroll/key-derivation even when the
                      binary offers the subcommand (they are always used when it does not)
  FOUNDRY_SOLC, FOUNDRY_OFFLINE
                      passed to `forge script`; unset, the solc-js shim (eth/tools/solc) is used
                      when it is present - set DEVNET_NATIVE_SOLC=1 to let forge use native solc
"""
